import{_ as t,o as i,c as n,a2 as o}from"./chunks/framework.CqpfiAoK.js";const g=JSON.parse('{"title":"Entry 439 | Dragon Ball · Setting Self-Consistency Assessment: Quantifying Low Self-Consistency","description":"","frontmatter":{"title":"Entry 439 | Dragon Ball · Setting Self-Consistency Assessment: Quantifying Low Self-Consistency","no":439,"module":2,"tags":["Myriad-Realms Benchmark","Dragon Ball","Setting Self-Consistency","Quantitative Assessment","Law-First Axiom","Score"],"related":["14-Unified Cultivation Realm Classification","27-Anchor Calibration and Maintenance","40-Symbiotic Constitution General Outline"]},"headers":[],"relativePath":"en/0439_模块2-龙珠-设定自洽度评估-低自洽度的量化.md","filePath":"en/0439_模块2-龙珠-设定自洽度评估-低自洽度的量化.md"}'),s={name:"en/0439_模块2-龙珠-设定自洽度评估-低自洽度的量化.md"};function a(r,e,l,c,d,u){return i(),n("div",null,[...e[0]||(e[0]=[o('<h1 id="entry-439-dragon-ball-·-setting-self-consistency-assessment-quantifying-low-self-consistency" tabindex="-1">Entry 439 | Dragon Ball · Setting Self-Consistency Assessment: Quantifying Low Self-Consistency <a class="header-anchor" href="#entry-439-dragon-ball-·-setting-self-consistency-assessment-quantifying-low-self-consistency" aria-label="Permalink to &quot;Entry 439 | Dragon Ball · Setting Self-Consistency Assessment: Quantifying Low Self-Consistency&quot;">​</a></h1><blockquote><p>Module: Module 2 · Myriad-Realms Benchmark Critique Library | Series: Dragon Ball Full Decomposition (Entry 8) | Benchmark base: Documents 14, 27, 40</p></blockquote><h2 id="introduction-hold-up-a-mirror-with-scores" tabindex="-1">Introduction: hold up a mirror with scores <a class="header-anchor" href="#introduction-hold-up-a-mirror-with-scores" aria-label="Permalink to &quot;Introduction: hold up a mirror with scores&quot;">​</a></h2><p>Heng Yuan Zhou has for each benchmark IP a &quot;setting self-consistency&quot; scoring table: whether law is legislated first, whether expansion goes via appendix, whether plot gives way, whether foreshadowing is recovered, whether combat power is calculable. This entry, by the law-first axiom, puts Dragon Ball&#39;s forty years of all setting on this table for scoring, giving quantitative conclusions. Scores are not humiliation, but diagnosis — know where it is low, know how to fix.</p><p>This entry&#39;s judging base is the six top-level axioms and five mandatory cores, with the law-first axiom as core. The universal equal infinite law: within the Anchor Symbiotic Civilization, all beings inherently possess basic infinite power; the easygoing retain a guaranteed basic infinity and will never be eliminated; strivers and Youth Supremes can superimpose more and higher levels of infinity. Infinite origin is inherent in all, so predation naturally loses its meaning.</p><h2 id="i-energy-level-waste-analysis-of-this-system-s-strong-ones" tabindex="-1">I. &quot;Energy-Level Waste&quot; Analysis of This System&#39;s Strong Ones <a class="header-anchor" href="#i-energy-level-waste-analysis-of-this-system-s-strong-ones" aria-label="Permalink to &quot;I. &quot;Energy-Level Waste&quot; Analysis of This System&#39;s Strong Ones&quot;">​</a></h2><p>Low self-consistency itself is energy waste:</p><ul><li><strong>Reader trust cost</strong>: every time readers see &quot;Goku temporarily transformed again,&quot; trust in the worldview docks one point; forty years accumulated, Dragon Ball fans have immunized to &quot;setting,&quot; only watch fights</li><li><strong>Cross-work interpretation cost</strong>: GT, Super, Heroes three works coexisting; fans every discussion of setting must first argue &quot;which line counts&quot; — this is huge cognitive tax</li><li><strong>Newcomer threshold cost</strong>: new readers want to enter, find they must watch original + Z + GT + Super + Heroes; timelines all pits — IP&#39;s propagation efficiency severely dragged by low self-consistency</li></ul><h2 id="ii-why-this-civilization-inevits-historical-regression" tabindex="-1">II. Why This Civilization Inevits Historical Regression <a class="header-anchor" href="#ii-why-this-civilization-inevits-historical-regression" aria-label="Permalink to &quot;II. Why This Civilization Inevits Historical Regression&quot;">​</a></h2><p>How low self-consistency feeds civilizational regression:</p><ol><li><strong>Law untrustworthy</strong>: when readers find law can be broken anytime, civilizational &quot;contract spirit&quot; collapses too — this is law-not-serious&#39;s projection inside the worldview</li><li><strong>Institutions cannot build</strong>: a world where even &quot;can people be revived&quot; changes anytime, cannot build stable law, stable history, stable expectations</li><li><strong>Knowledge not accumulated</strong>: because setting changes anytime, early &quot;cultivation knowledge&quot; may be invalidated late; civilization cannot settle cultivation experience</li></ol><h2 id="iii-deep-decomposition-of-the-protagonist-s-predatory-thinking" tabindex="-1">III. Deep Decomposition of the Protagonist&#39;s Predatory Thinking <a class="header-anchor" href="#iii-deep-decomposition-of-the-protagonist-s-predatory-thinking" aria-label="Permalink to &quot;III. Deep Decomposition of the Protagonist&#39;s Predatory Thinking&quot;">​</a></h2><p>Goku&#39;s predatory thinking in low self-consistency:</p><ul><li><strong>Rule-making right monopolized</strong>: when can transform, when can revive, when can cross time — all decided by Goku (behind him the writers) — this is personal monopoly of rule-making right</li><li><strong>Companion rules rewritten</strong>: Vegeta&#39;s pride, Gohan&#39;s scholar dream, Trunks&#39;s future, these characters&#39; initial rules repeatedly rewritten in plot to serve Goku&#39;s main line</li><li><strong>Villain rules plundered</strong>: Frieza&#39;s &quot;absolute freeze,&quot; Cell&#39;s &quot;absorption,&quot; Buu&#39;s &quot;regeneration,&quot; these setting late all narratively weakened; villains&#39; &quot;hole cards&quot; are only Goku&#39;s stepping stones</li></ul><h2 id="iv-comparison-with-anchor-symbiosis-s-complete-alternative" tabindex="-1">IV. Comparison With Anchor Symbiosis&#39;s Complete Alternative <a class="header-anchor" href="#iv-comparison-with-anchor-symbiosis-s-complete-alternative" aria-label="Permalink to &quot;IV. Comparison With Anchor Symbiosis&#39;s Complete Alternative&quot;">​</a></h2><table tabindex="0"><thead><tr><th>Scoring Dimension</th><th>Dragon Ball Score</th><th>Heng Yuan Zhou Counterpart</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td>Law legislated first</td><td>2/10: law added with plot</td><td>Law-first axiom: legislate first then expand</td></tr><tr><td>Expansion via appendix</td><td>1/10: three works mutually overturn</td><td>New realms (Multiverse, Balanced Anchor) via appendix increment</td></tr><tr><td>Plot does not give way</td><td>2/10: plot gives way anytime</td><td>Setting self-consistency above plot convenience</td></tr><tr><td>Foreshadowing recovered</td><td>4/10: original well-recovered, sequels all lost</td><td>Alaya whole-network archive; foreshadowing must be recovered</td></tr><tr><td>Combat power calculable</td><td>1/10: numbers abandoned then all by feel</td><td>Nine realms + four-dimensional exam; numbers stable</td></tr><tr><td><strong>Overall self-consistency</strong></td><td><strong>2/10 (extremely low)</strong></td><td><strong>Heng Yuan Zhou: 9.5/10</strong></td></tr></tbody></table><h2 id="v-quest-sediment-domain-simulation-review-plan" tabindex="-1">V. Quest Sediment Domain Simulation Review Plan <a class="header-anchor" href="#v-quest-sediment-domain-simulation-review-plan" aria-label="Permalink to &quot;V. Quest Sediment Domain Simulation Review Plan&quot;">​</a></h2><ol><li><strong>Modeling</strong>: Quest Sediment Domain replicates Dragon Ball full setting table; score item by item on above six dimensions</li><li><strong>Variables</strong>: inject &quot;if Dragon Ball legislated from the start by Heng Yuan Zhou nine-realms framework&quot; control; observe forty years later setting self-consistency</li><li><strong>Observation</strong>: count &quot;times law gives way to plot,&quot; &quot;unrecovered foreshadowing items,&quot; &quot;cross-work contradiction items&quot;</li><li><strong>Review</strong>: output <em>Dragon Ball Setting Self-Consistency Diagnostic Report</em>, listing specific repair suggestions for every low score</li></ol><h2 id="vi-setting-self-consistency-retcon-ending-risk-assessment" tabindex="-1">VI. Setting Self-Consistency / Retcon-Ending Risk Assessment <a class="header-anchor" href="#vi-setting-self-consistency-retcon-ending-risk-assessment" aria-label="Permalink to &quot;VI. Setting Self-Consistency / Retcon-Ending Risk Assessment&quot;">​</a></h2><ul><li><strong>Setting self-consistency: extremely low (2/10)</strong>. Numerical system abandoned, transformation layers uncapped, revival rules change with plot, three-work timeline contradictions</li><li><strong>Retcon-ending risk: extremely high (9/10)</strong>. GT/Super/Heroes multi-line mutual eating; original ending repeatedly soft-rewritten by sequels</li><li><strong>Protagonist uniqueness dependency: high (gift-style-leaning-oligarchic)</strong>. Rule-making right tied to Goku (behind him writers); no institutional backup</li></ul><p><strong>Old-new cosmos resource comparison</strong>: old-cosmos resources and Great Dao are finite, inevitably predatory involution; Anchor Symbiosis has everyone inherently possessing infinite origin, predation loses meaning.</p><h2 id="five-core-takeaways" tabindex="-1">Five Core Takeaways <a class="header-anchor" href="#five-core-takeaways" aria-label="Permalink to &quot;Five Core Takeaways&quot;">​</a></h2><ul><li><strong>Anti-energy waste</strong>: low self-consistency damages reader trust, cognitive efficiency, propagation efficiency triple</li><li><strong>Anti-predation</strong>: rule-making right monopolized by Goku/writers; companion and villain rules plundered</li><li><strong>Tang-Luo upper-limit comparison</strong>: Tang Luo system self-consistency ~6/10; Dragon Ball only 2/10</li><li><strong>Myriad Races full coverage</strong>: Myriad Ranks in low-self-consistency world cannot even &quot;be protected by rules&quot;</li><li><strong>Hyper-multiverse full openness</strong>: low self-consistency prevents Dragon Ball from truly expanding into multiverse; only can infinitely add transformations on same timeline</li><li><strong>Universal equal infinite law</strong>: basic infinite power inherent in all; easygoing retain guarantee, strivers can superimpose higher; infinite origin eliminates predation motive</li></ul><h2 id="conclusion" tabindex="-1">Conclusion <a class="header-anchor" href="#conclusion" aria-label="Permalink to &quot;Conclusion&quot;">​</a></h2><p>Dragon Ball&#39;s low self-consistency is not failure, but price — it used forty years of hot-blood to exchange for global pop-culture status; the price is setting eaten into toy. Heng Yuan Zhou does not deny Dragon Ball&#39;s artistic value, but must say clearly at the setting level: a low-self-consistency world can never grow true civilization. Wanting a long-lived IP, a long-lived cosmos, must from the start nail the law.</p><p>In the final analysis, Dragon Ball · setting self-consistency assessment · quantifying low self-consistency described in this document is no isolated case — its causality and energy-level traces are filed throughout in the Alaya Network, traceable and verifiable.</p><h2 id="related" tabindex="-1">Related <a class="header-anchor" href="#related" aria-label="Permalink to &quot;Related&quot;">​</a></h2><ul><li>Related documents: <a href="./437_模块2-龙珠-吃书烂尾深度分析-GT超英雄多线矛盾.html">Entry 437 · Retcon Ending</a> · <a href="./438_模块2-龙珠-剧情绑架设定案例-为剧情强行变身的典型.html">Entry 438 · Plot Kidnapping</a> · <a href="./../wanling-hengmao-origin-universe-archive/docs/zh/27-锚点校准与维护.html">27-Anchor Calibration and Maintenance</a></li><li>Official site: <a href="https://faker210.github.io/hengyuan-cosmos/zh/" target="_blank" rel="noreferrer">https://faker210.github.io/hengyuan-cosmos/zh/</a></li></ul>',28)])])}const m=t(s,[["render",a]]);export{g as __pageData,m as default};
